Subject: [RFC PATCH 0/2] optimize: ksmbd workqueue optimize

This series changes the ksmbd I/O workqueue from WQ_PERCPU to
WQ_UNBOUND with non-strict CPU affinity. The aim is to preserve CPU
locality while allowing workers to use other CPUs when requests are
concentrated on a few CPUs.

Huiwen He (2):
  workqueue: export workqueue attribute helpers for modules
  ksmbd: use a non-strict CPU-affine unbound I/O workqueue

 fs/smb/server/ksmbd_work.c | 50 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 kernel/workqueue.c         |  3 +++
